@startuml Builder Pattern - Class Structure

!define ABSTRACT class abstract

package "Product" {
    class Pizza {
        -size: str
        -crust: str
        -toppings: List[str]
        +__init__(): None
        +add_topping(topping: str): None
        +set_size(size: str): None
        +set_crust(crust: str): None
        +get_description(): str
        +get_price(): float
        +__str__(): str
        +__repr__(): str
    }
}

package "Builder" {
    class PizzaBuilder {
        -_pizza: Optional[Pizza]
        +__init__(): None
        +reset(): PizzaBuilder
        +set_size(size: str): PizzaBuilder
        +set_crust(crust: str): PizzaBuilder
        +add_cheese(cheese_type: str): PizzaBuilder
        +add_bacon(): PizzaBuilder
        +add_pineapple(): PizzaBuilder
        +add_mushrooms(mushroom_type: str): PizzaBuilder
        +add_seafood(seafood_type: str): PizzaBuilder
        +add_pepperoni(): PizzaBuilder
        +add_vegetables(vegetable: str): PizzaBuilder
        +add_custom_topping(topping: str): PizzaBuilder
        +build(): Pizza
        +get_current_pizza_info(): str
    }
}

package "Client" {
    class ClientCode {
        +main(): None
        +interactive_demo(): None
    }
}

PizzaBuilder --> Pizza : builds
ClientCode ..> PizzaBuilder : uses
ClientCode ..> Pizza : receives

note right of PizzaBuilder::build
  Build Method Inside Builder:
  - Returns the constructed Pizza
  - Resets builder for next use
  - Core method of Builder pattern
end note

note left of PizzaBuilder
  Fluent Interface:
  - Each method returns self
  - Enables method chaining
  - Makes code readable

  Required Toppings:
  - Cheese
  - Bacon
  - Pineapple
  - Mushrooms
  - Seafood
end note

note bottom of Pizza
  Product Class:
  - Stores pizza configuration
  - Calculates price based on size/toppings
  - Provides description formatting
end note

@enduml
